# A fixture file's BYTES are the document (see README.md, "Reading a
# fixture"): the manifest records a sha256 over the file itself, with no
# convention to interpret first. Line-ending churn here is corpus
# corruption, not formatting — every recorded digest would move at once,
# and the failure would surface on someone else's machine as a
# specification defect that is not one.
#
# The documents happen to contain no newline at all, so normalisation is
# currently a no-op. This file exists so that stays true by rule rather
# than by luck, and so a future broad rule in a parent .gitattributes
# cannot silently take the corpus with it.
*.json -text

# The index is a hand-formatted document for humans, and is not itself a
# specified wire shape.
manifest.json text eol=lf

# The emitter and the checker are ordinary source.
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.md  text eol=lf
